## Example

### Input

"Create a feature to add a new transaction"

### Output

#### Explanation

This feature allows users to create financial transactions. Logic is handled in the backend service, while the frontend only handles input and submission.

#### Backend (NestJS)

```ts
// transaction.dto.ts
export class CreateTransactionDto {
  amount: number;
  type: 'INCOME' | 'EXPENSE';
  categoryId: string;
  accountId: string;
}
```

```ts
// transaction.service.ts
async create(dto: CreateTransactionDto, userId: string) {
  return this.prisma.transaction.create({
    data: {
      ...dto,
      userId,
      date: new Date()
    }
  });
}
```

```ts
// transaction.controller.ts
@Post()
create(@Body() dto: CreateTransactionDto, @Req() req) {
  return this.transactionService.create(dto, req.user.id);
}
```

#### Frontend (React)

```tsx
const form = useForm({
  resolver: zodResolver(schema)
});

const onSubmit = async (data) => {
  await api.post('/transactions', data);
};
```

#### Notes

- Backend handles all business rules
- Frontend only sends validated data
- Prisma ensures database consistency

